From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: odonnellmatt <odonnellmatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 10:01:31 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ios/pad: Adjust Gamepad Layout, an in-game editor for the
 touch controls

The groups of the touch controls (DM_TOUCH_GROUPS, the previous change) are
set in the game. The gear's Controller layout menu holds Adjust Gamepad
Layout below 2D, 3D and Tap (in 2D and 3D: Tap has no controls). It opens
the layout editor over the game (DmGamepad.m, "The layout editor", on the
rules of DmPadEditing.h):

- Every group is outlined, with its name on a tag. A tap chooses one. A
  drag moves it once the finger has gone 8 points, snapping to the edges
  and the middle of its area. A pinch with two fingers on it, or the
  panel's slider or - and +, resizes it. A thumb resting elsewhere neither
  stops a drag nor starts a pinch, and a touch on the panel never moves a
  group under it.
- The panel (DmPadEditor.m, a small dark card the player can drag by its
  title) has, above the chosen group's row, a two-way choice: Both sides
  together (the default: the shoulders of both sides, and the left stick
  with A B X Y, move and size together, so one drag lowers the whole top
  row) or Each side on its own. The choice is kept per layout and saved
  with it. Picking Both sides together while the two sides are apart moves
  nothing; the next move or size of either takes the other to its mirrored
  place, or is refused there for want of room. For a group with no mirror
  image (the D-pad in 3D, and - with the menu button and +) the choice is
  dimmed, still showing the layout's, so the panel keeps its height. The
  panel also has All controls, Save for All games or This game (in the
  shell), Reset to default (for this game also "Same as All games"),
  Cancel and Done. It is placed again after a rotation or a new window
  size.
- A spot with no room is drawn red under the finger and the group goes
  back when the finger lifts. A size stops where the group meets another.
  The panel says why, once per gesture, with a warning haptic.
- While the editor is open the game keeps running but is told it lost the
  focus, as for the quit prompt (front_ios_overlay_focus), so a game that
  pauses there pauses. The touch gamepad releases every key and sends
  nothing, no touch reaches the game, and physical controllers keep
  playing. The controls show even while a controller hides them.
- VoiceOver: each group is an adjustable element with Move up, down, left
  and right. The elements are made once, so the focus stays on them. The
  choice is named "Move left and right groups"; dimmed, it is one element
  that says why ("This group has no matching group on the other side.").
- Drawing follows the groups: labels, roundings and the gear's symbol take
  each group's size, and the stick's travel goes with its ring.

Done saves DM_TOUCH_GROUPS. A front end that hosts games in its own process
keeps the value through three hooks the engine finds with dlsym
(dm_shell_touch_groups_save, _load and _forget, docs/frontends.md), for
every game or for this game, and passes the value in effect at the next
start, with DM_TOUCH_GROUPS_OWN=1 for a game's own. A game's own app keeps
it in its preferences as launcher.DM_TOUCH_GROUPS. When the player picks
the other scope, Done replaces only the layouts the editor showed or the
player changed and keeps the others as that scope holds them. Done with
nothing changed saves nothing. The menu item's words are the third line of
DM_GAME_MENU_TEXT and the editor's are DM_PAD_EDIT_TEXT (27 lines, in
DmPadEditing.h's order); without them the editor is in English. With
nothing stored the touch controls draw and take touches as before.

Docs: settings.md (In-game menu), playing.md, frontends.md (the hooks),
env_switches.tsv (DM_TOUCH_GROUPS, DM_TOUCH_GROUPS_OWN, DM_PAD_EDIT_TEXT,
DM_GAME_MENU_TEXT). DmPadEditor.m is added to the shell framework's sources
and to the Duo harness.

Checked here (Linux, no Apple SDK): DmGamepad.m and DmPadEditor.m pass
clang -fsyntax-only -fobjc-arc against declaration stubs of the Apple
names they use; test_pad_geometry.py (clang -Wall -Werror), with
pad_groups_check.m's check_mirror_choice (on every screen in 2D and 3D:
which groups the choice is for, linked exactly when it applies, each side
on its own moves one side, picking Both sides together moves nothing,
Reset and another scope keep it, Done saves it) and the 27 lines' order;
the same checks under gcc ASan and UBSan; env_switches.py --check,
test_docs.py. With no groups the pad is byte-identical to the base's (a
dump of every geometry field and the hit test, 3,528 cases, same md5).
New Duo harness tests: one drag lowers both shoulder clusters by 250
points on an 11-inch iPad held sideways and the moved keys take their
touches; Each side on its own moves one cluster and is saved; a touch on
the panel moves no group; a resting thumb leaves a drag alone; Cancel keeps
the layout from before and saves nothing; a pinch takes the stick to 150 %
with its travel.

Run on a Mac, on the author's own tree (this series' feature code on
another base), with the whole series applied (the Duo harness links again
only from its last change): Xcode built it, the harness's seven
testLayoutEditor cases passed on Simulators of an iPhone SE (3rd generation), an iPhone 17, an
iPhone 17 Pro Max and an 11-inch iPad, held sideways and upright, in
English, German and French; the shell with the editor was installed and
played on an 11-inch iPad. Not run: this exact tree on a Mac (that is the
pull request's CI and mac-verify), a real iPhone, a game's own app.

Front-ends: new: a front end that hosts games in its own process keeps the in-game layout editor's groups by exporting dm_shell_touch_groups_save, _load and _forget, and passes DM_TOUCH_GROUPS (with DM_TOUCH_GROUPS_OWN=1 for a game's own); it may pass DM_PAD_EDIT_TEXT (27 lines) and a third DM_GAME_MENU_TEXT line (docs/frontends.md)

Upstream-Status: pending [builds on 0020 and 0040: the seedds/nxnative pull request follows once they are upstream]
Reason: players move and resize the touch controls by groups in the game (gear, Controller layout, Adjust Gamepad Layout), saved for all games or for one game
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#1397 (the feature issue, to be opened before the pull request)
