+// ---- The layout editor ("Adjust Gamepad Layout") ----
+// Opened from the in-game menu (GameMenu.swift: the gear › Controller layout › Adjust Gamepad Layout) in the 2D and 3D layouts. While it is open the game
+// keeps running but is told it lost the focus, as for the quit prompt (front_ios_overlay_focus: a game that pauses then pauses, as on a Switch's HOME menu),
+// the touch gamepad sends nothing and no touch reaches the game: every touch on the gamepad edits it, one on the panel is the panel's. Physical
+// controllers keep playing as before.
+//   A tap chooses a group (DmPadGeometry.h's DM_PAD_G_*: each outlined, its name on a tag), a drag moves it once the finger has gone a few points (its box
+//   snaps to the edges and the middle of its area), a pinch of two fingers on it, the panel's slider or − and + resize it. DmPadEditing.h's fingers decide
+//   which finger drags and when two pinch: a thumb resting elsewhere neither stops a drag nor starts a pinch. The panel (DmPadEditor.m) also has, above
+//   the chosen group's row, the choice Both sides together (the default: the shoulders of both sides, and the left stick with A B X Y, move together, and
+//   size together as far as each has room) or Each side on its own, per layout, dimmed for the D-pad and − + (no mirror image); all controls' size, where
+//   Done saves (in the shell: all games or this game), Reset to default (the layout on screen back to the built-in one; for this game also "Same as All
+//   games"), Cancel (the layout from before) and Done.
+//   Every change goes through DmPadEditing.h's rules: a spot that does not fit is drawn red under the finger and the group goes back when it lifts, a size
+//   stops where the group meets another, and the panel says why, once per gesture.
